        "content": "## I'm a note \n**Double click** to edit me. [Guide](https://docs.n8n.io/workflows/components/sticky-notes/)\n\n\n## Data Cleanup\nWhat it means: Fixing, formatting, or removing incorrect, corrupted, or duplicate data.Why this fits: \n- The .trim() method cleans up human entry errors (like accidental spaces or hidden tabs) so systems can match text accurately.\n\n## Data Manipulation\nWhat it means: Modifying or adapting data to make it readable, structured, or compatible with a destination system.Why this fits: \n- The .toUpperCase() method transforms the actual appearance and casing of the text to enforce a standardized format.\n\n## Data Engineering\nWhat it means: The overarching practice of building pipelines to move, transform, and store data.Why this fits: \n\n- Cleanup and manipulation are steps inside the Transformation (T) phase of an ETL/ELT pipeline built by a data engineer.If you are building an automation pipeline, let me know:Where is the data coming from? (e.g., forms, emails, databases)Where is it going? (e.g., CRMs, Google Sheets, APIs)",
